# SPA routing. Every non-file path renders the app shell.
#
# ⚠️ KNOWN HAZARD, deliberately left in place because Cloudflare Pages gives us
# no way to close it here.
#
# This rule also answers a MISSING /app-assets/*.js with index.html at HTTP 200.
# Combined with the immutable caching in _headers, that is what took
# dev.utahpros.app down on 2026-07-27: during a deployment swap an edge node
# requested a chunk that had not uploaded yet, cached the HTML answer under a
# .js URL for a year, and every client that touched that PoP got a permanently
# blank page — browsers refuse text/html for <script type="module">, so the
# entry graph never instantiates and nothing throws.
#
# Two attempts to make a missing asset 404 here BOTH FAILED on a real preview
# deployment (2026-07-27):
#   /app-assets/* /asset-missing.html 404   -> ignored; Pages 308-normalizes
#                                              .html, and a redirecting target
#                                              makes the rule fall through
#   /app-assets/* /asset-missing 404        -> also ignored; a missing asset
#                                              still returned index.html + 200
# Do not re-add a variant of these without verifying it on a preview build
# first. A rule that looks protective but is inert is worse than none.
#
# What actually protects users is therefore NOT prevention but recovery:
#   - the boot guard in index.html repairs poisoned cache entries with
#     fetch(url, {cache:'reload'}) and reloads, which works on Safari where
#     /reset's Clear-Site-Data does not;
#   - build.assetsDir (vite.config.js) can be moved to retire a poisoned URL
#     namespace outright, as was done once on 2026-07-27.
/* /index.html 200
